    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d787">

                <pb facs="0942" n="932" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg932"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">562.8F4/35: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-03T18:00:00+01:00">January 3, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 3—1:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. Reference Embassy’s 17, January 3<anchor n="6" xml:id="d787-f1"/> regarding
                    delay in Kellogg’s arrival. Embassy has now been informed that Dr. Kellogg’s
                    plane is still in Bermuda and he cannot therefore reach London before night of
                    January 6 at earliest. While Embassy understands conference will probably
                    adjourn on 4th to reconvene on 6th, <pb facs="0943" n="933" xml:id="pg933"/> it
                    is believed it will be difficult to delay any longer. In view of British
                    expectation of short duration of conference, it is quite possible Dr. Kellogg
                    might not arrive until after its final adjournment. In these circumstances does
                    Department have any special instructions?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
